{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-80396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2xy{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043864/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae75f884af0d53a49469c08c5a707fd7d42d7edc42e8ef3e94a8849586691bcc"} {"question" "q-80396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot ({e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}+2{x}^{2}{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}) \\\\  & =2y(1+2{x}^{2}){e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043864/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae75f884af0d53a49469c08c5a707fd7d42d7edc42e8ef3e94a8849586691bcc"} {"question" "q-80396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043864/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d47d6331b62b30213ae5ab9c9023e7287a004897bc643e2e48e45a8227b504cf"} {"question" "q-80396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043864/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae75f884af0d53a49469c08c5a707fd7d42d7edc42e8ef3e94a8849586691bcc"} {"question" "q-80396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "va